  "backend": "comfyui",
  "category": "edit-images",
  "description": "Inpaint via an OpenAI-compatible /v3/images/edits API served by OpenVINO Model Server",
  "extendedDescription": "Runs inpainting through ComfyUI using OVMS multipart /images/edits (image + mask + prompt). Use the mask editor: painted regions become transparent in the PNG sent to ComfyUI, which matches OVMS (white in the mask image = area to repaint). Serve an inpainting-capable model on OVMS (default id is stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-inpainting; your server may use a different id, e.g. from --source_model). Default API base URL http://127.0.0.1:8000/v3. If you run without painting a mask (opaque image only), the node calls the same edits API without a mask file (image-to-image) using strength and rng_seed; use a base diffusion model on OVMS for that path\u2014dedicated inpainting checkpoints may only accept masked requests.",
  "mediaType": "image",
  "toolCategory": "edit-images",
  "toolInstructions": "Load a source image, open the mask editor, paint the region to change, then describe what should appear there. Match resolution to your OVMS model (often 512\u00d7512 for SD1.5 inpainting).",
